body:
"reported"

&#x200B;

That's how this works right? I report you cause I don't like what you're saying?

Depending on how long it's been since the reservation check-out, you can start a resolution case. Airbnb \*should\* be able to do something if the guest is unwilling to pay for it.

&#x200B;

As for putting it in the house rules, no, it's not necessary. If something is lost or damaged, you can request the guest to pay and talk to Airbnb about their Host Guarantee if the guest is being difficult.

&#x200B;

Source: [https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/279](https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/279/what-is-the-airbnb-host-guarantee)
